+## What the browser keeps
+
+None of it is sent anywhere except inside the requests described above. Every key is in
+`apps/web/lib/session.ts` or `apps/web/lib/offline.ts`.
+
+- `sl_client_token` (localStorage): the random browser token. Only its hash is sent.
+- `sl_open_session` (localStorage): the id of an unfinished test, the lesson card and when it
+  was last saved, so a reload resumes. Cleared when the person leaves the end screen, and not
+  picked up again after 3 hours (`OPEN_SESSION_HOURS`).
+- `sl_contributor_token` and `sl_contributor_saved_at` (localStorage): only after "Keep my
+  score". The token rides on creek checks from this browser for 90 days, the life of the score
+  (`CONTRIBUTOR_TOKEN_DAYS`), and is then forgotten. Before a check is sent the app names the
+  first four characters of the token and offers "Not me", which forgets it.
+- `sl_saved_spots` (localStorage): the names and ids of spots this browser checked.
+- `sl_src` and `sl_landing_guess` (sessionStorage): the link label and the landing page choice,
+  gone when the tab closes.
+- IndexedDB `second-look`, store `queue`: creek checks that wait to be sent, with their answers,
+  the spot, the contributor token and the photos. A check is removed once it is sent. A check
+  the server refused stays until the person taps Try again or Delete on `/check`; a timeout, a
+  429 or a 5xx is not a refusal, so that check waits and goes on the next try. Photos are
+  redrawn on the phone before they are queued, which leaves the camera's EXIF behind, and a
+  photo the phone cannot redraw is refused when it is picked.
+
+One browser counts as one person: it keeps one arm, and only its first completed test counts.
+On a shared phone or tablet the next person taps "Start fresh" (on `/privacy`, on the last test
+screen, or when `/t` picks up a test this browser started), which clears all of the above.
+
